# What `synoik-lifecycle` still means on a driver that did not record it.
#
# Generated from a run, never transcribed from a diff. A corpus replays the guest's memory type
# indices verbatim, and this one's guest chose them out of KosmicKrisp's heaps; the same indices
# on anv are device-local, so nothing the content half of the score describes is addressable here
# and its `mem`, `blob` and `iosurface` lines measure nothing. Those are left unpinned rather than
# pinned at zero. What is here is acceptance, which means the same thing on any driver -- see
# `compare_lines` in harness/replay/rs/src/main.rs and "What Linux scores, and what it cannot" in
# harness/README.md.
